# ===================================================================
# Phase 14 — R Analysis
# ===================================================================
#
# Reproducible R-based re-analysis of the demand, variability,
# inventory-scenario and forecasting evidence produced by Phases 11–13,
# independently verifying it across languages. The workflow consumes the
# compact analytical outputs generated by Phase 13 plus the stored Phase 12
# validation forecasts, rather than reloading the full integrated dataset
# unnecessarily.
#
# The project root is discovered by walking up from the working directory
# looking for `pyproject.toml` and `docs/`, and can be overridden — together
# with the input and output directories — through R_ANALYSIS_PROJECT_ROOT,
# R_ANALYSIS_INPUT_DIR and R_ANALYSIS_OUTPUT_DIR, which is how the automated
# tests run the complete workflow into a temporary directory.
#
# Every validation result is recorded in a machine-readable quality report
# (`r_analysis_quality_report.csv`) that gates the run. The workflow
# definition ends in `main()`, invoked only when this file is executed as a
# script; the R Markdown report sources the file and calls `main()`, so the
# report and the script verify the same evidence.
#
# Python remains the primary forecasting implementation. R is used here as
# an independent analytical, validation and reporting workflow.

